@startuml fixed-point
' The fixed point of the Y.
'
' The Y of the name is the Y-combinator: person -> environment -> agent ->
' environment.  This picture gives that sentence a shape, and ties it to the
' one thing of the kernel that makes it a loop: the delegation.  A child of a
' delegation runs in a session of its own, with a journal of its own, with the
' tools of its preset and at a depth of its own.
'
' The limits are on the picture on purpose: the depth of the tree is bounded,
' the time of a child is bounded and the budget of a child is bounded.  A
' recursion that is not bounded is not a fixed point, it is a fork bomb.
'
' The fixed point is the last step of the picture: the agent changes the code
' and the check that hold it, and the check passes afterwards.

|Human|
start
:give the task to the environment;

|Environment|
:holds the files, the buffers\nand the checks of the project;

|Agent|
:read the environment;
:call the tools of the kernel\n(read, edit, bash, git_status, todo_list);
:change the environment;
note right
  The live state of Emacs is read
  and written here
  lib/yeah-emacs.el:62
  lib/yeah-emacs.el:120
end note

|Environment|
:the change is the new environment;

|Agent|
if (does the task need a child?) then (yes)
  :delegate names an agent preset;
  note right
    The preset is a file: a name, a model,
    the tools and the depth
    lib/yeah-agent.el:131
    lib/yeah-delegate.el:219
  end note
  :the child runs in a session of its own,\nwith its own journal, its own tools\nand its own depth;
  :the child changes the environment too;
  note right
    The depth of the tree is bounded,
    the time of a child is bounded,
    the budget of a child is bounded
    lib/yeah-subagent.el:156
    lib/yeah-subagent.el:313
  end note
else (no)
  :the agent keeps the tools of its own;
endif

|Agent|
:run the check of the environment;
if (does the check pass?) then (yes)
  :the environment holds the repair:\nthe agent fixed its own code\nand its own check;
else (no)
  :read the failure\nand change the environment again;
endif

|Human|
:see what the environment holds;
stop
@enduml
